      "type": "text",
      "width": "full",
      "heading": "THE WRONG DIMENSION WAS THE LESSON",
      "body": "Mighty Pebble came out of a list of deliberately small prototype ideas. The premise was a clicker game in which you play a god, gather resources directly from the world and buy upgrades that change what the world can produce.\n\nThe central mistake was prototyping it in 3D. Similar ideas such as Clicky Islands and Clickyland are clearer and more immediate because they embrace a 2D presentation. Realizing that was useful: 2D stopped feeling like a compromise and became an important part of how we think about future projects.",
